          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The following terminology for the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+morphism"}> higher
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in the
            %a{:href => "monad#BicategoryOfMonads"} 2-category of monads
            have appeared in the literature or are otherwise sensible:
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th author(s)
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a{:href => "#Maranda66"}> Maranda 1966
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Maranda68"} 1968
                  %br/
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Frei69"} Frei 1969
                  %br/
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Pumplün70"} Pumplün 1970
                  %br/
                  %a{:href => "#Borceux94"} Borceux 1994
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} “morphisms of monads”
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} —
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a{:href => "#Street72"} Street 1972
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} “monad functors”
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} “monad functor transformations”
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a{:href => "#Moggi89"} Moggi 1989
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} “monad-morphisms”
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} —
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a{:href => "#Espinosa95"}> Espinosa 1995
                  ,
                  %br/
                  %a{:href => "#LiangHudakJones95"} Liang, Hudak &amp; Jones 1995
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+transformers"}> monad transformers
                  ”
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^1
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} —
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a{:href => "#LackStreet02"} Lack &amp; Street 2002
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} “monad morphisms”
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} “monad transformations”
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} —
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  “monad
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  “monad
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} —
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+natural+transformation"}> lax transformations
                  ” of monads
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modifications"}> modifications
                  ” of monads
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^1
            \: Notice here that the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+transformers"}> monad transformers
            ” in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Espinosa95"} Espinosa 1995
            %a{:href => "#LiangHudakJones95"} Liang, Hudak &amp; Jones 1995
            (as commonly understood now in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haskell"} Haskell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
            families constituting a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+endofunctor"} pointed endofunctor
            on the category of monads (made explicit in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Winitzki22"} Winitzki 2022 p. 474
          %p
            Of course, monads are often referred to via their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            = succeed "," do
              %em transformations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            = succeed "." do
              %em natural transformation of functors, respecting their monad structure
          %p
            Similarly, if one thinks of monads as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functors"} lax functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to Cat
            (which is where they get their name from!, see
            = succeed ")" do
